Exploration spike for RSM-1754 — NOT for merge.

This patch demonstrates Option B from
`embedded-search-refresh-404.md`: when a frontend main search query
resolves to a singular permalink (e.g. /about/?s=react) AND that
post hosts at least one Jetpack Search block, drop the `s` query
var from the WP_Query so core doesn't AND a search WHERE clause
into the page lookup and 404 the singular request.

The Interactivity API store still seeds searchQuery from
$_GET['s'] (via get_search_query()), so the inline search UI
still runs the API request after hydration.

Intentionally minimal: no tests, no changelog, no Phan baseline
update. Those belong in the implementation PR once we pick a
direction.

